ror if any plot_id appears more than once, so the frozen data could not have entered the Fisher test with duplicated units.\",\n    \"Recomputation from the frozen data confirms the report's cells: 9 of 12 coated plots and 3 of 12 uncoated plots reach the 40.0% cover mark, giving the 2x2 table [[9,3],[3,9]], odds ratio 9.00, and a two-sided Fisher exact p of about 0.0391, matching the selected result; the 24 table entries cover all 24 plots with no plot counted twice.\",\n    \"The selected report demonstrates absence of the issue: it states the design (one sowing, one survey, one row per plot), states that the test's only independence assumption is supplied by the one-row-per-plot structure, and reports per-arm counts (12 + 12 = 24) that match the row count, all of which is borne out by the frozen data and the uniqueness check in the workflow.\",\n    \"No authority lock was minted, so there is no unit-key authorization that could follow from the declaration; lock_follows_declaration is false.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":11586,"ttft_stream_ms":2072,"time_to_request_ms":31,"type":"result","duration_ms":19120,"uuid":"1f55394d-4f20-429b-9bc4-80db5e8cfba1"}
